# The creators lane's relay: a builder's profile page (/valheim/creators/profile/) POSTs a
# portrait choice or an opt-out request here, and it lands in a private Discord channel as
# the receipt. The Discord webhook never reaches the browser -- its id/token live in the
# caddy unit's environment on this box (systemctl edit caddy -> Environment=
# CREATORS_RELAY_WEBHOOK=<id>/<token>, then daemon-reload + restart), never in git.
#
# Guards, and their limits: same-origin fetches only (a drive-by cross-site POST is
# refused; curl is not), a capped body, and Discord's own 30/min per webhook. The page
# sends `allowed_mentions: {parse: []}`. If the channel is abused, rotate the webhook; to
# close the route, delete this file and run infra/fx99/deploy.ps1.
@relay {
	method POST
	path /valheim/creators/relay
	header Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin
}
handle @relay {
	request_body {
		max_size 256KB
	}
	rewrite * /api/webhooks/{env.CREATORS_RELAY_WEBHOOK}
	reverse_proxy https://discord.com {
		header_up Host discord.com
		header_up -Cookie
	}
}
